1
00:00:11,365 --> 00:00:14,452
FROM ME TO YOU 2ND SEASON

2
00:01:01,082 --> 00:01:02,208
VALENTINE

3
00:01:53,634 --> 00:01:57,304
- Yummy as always!
-"Yummy," huh?

4
00:01:57,388 --> 00:02:02,101
Oh, uh... Ayane, would you like one too?

5
00:02:02,351 --> 00:02:05,312
- Thanks. Here's one in return.
- Thank you.

6
00:02:05,396 --> 00:02:08,399
So? Have you gotten
used to your new seat yet?

7
00:02:08,482 --> 00:02:09,608
Oh, yeah!

8
00:02:11,652 --> 00:02:17,366
Our winter break has ended and it's
now January. We had a seating change.

9
00:02:17,449 --> 00:02:23,414
Maybe I'm just thinking too far into
it... but Takahashi, the girl behind me...

10
00:02:25,207 --> 00:02:27,543
She plays around with
me even during class.

11
00:02:27,626 --> 00:02:30,713
Cootchie-cootchie-cootchie-cootchie-coo...

12
00:02:30,796 --> 00:02:33,883
Even my neighbor, Yagi,
will talk to me sometimes.

13
00:02:33,966 --> 00:02:36,969
I get sleep paralysis like an alarming
amount, but do you think I'll be okay?

14
00:02:37,052 --> 00:02:40,055
- Yes, you should be fine.
- That's a relief!

15
00:02:40,890 --> 00:02:44,310
Compared to before, I feel like
I'm not being avoided near as much.

16
00:02:44,393 --> 00:02:47,813
That's awesome! Thanks to everyone.

17
00:02:48,731 --> 00:02:52,026
- Sawako's famous "thank-you" time!
- But she sure worked her way up

18
00:02:52,109 --> 00:02:55,404
- to this didn't she? It's so good!
- Even though our seats are apart now, it

19
00:02:55,487 --> 00:02:58,199
doesn't mean that I'm back to square one
at all.

20
00:02:58,282 --> 00:03:01,035
- I know! Right?
- I'm still making progress.

21
00:03:02,828 --> 00:03:04,538
What you think, Sawako?

22
00:03:04,622 --> 00:03:05,456
Good! Yummy!

23
00:03:06,165 --> 00:03:07,082
Yeah! Right?!

24
00:03:09,460 --> 00:03:12,004
- No way, for real?
- Yeah, like this!

25
00:03:13,631 --> 00:03:18,636
Although if I said, "I wasn't
lonely at all"... it would be a lie.

26
00:03:18,719 --> 00:03:23,057
She doesn't smile easily, does she?

27
00:03:26,936 --> 00:03:30,689
- Huh?
- Yeah, that move was incredible... Huh?

28
00:03:32,816 --> 00:03:34,318
- Oh, it's just Sadako.
- That's enough.

29
00:03:34,401 --> 00:03:37,613
- You, uh scared me.
- Yeah.

30
00:03:37,696 --> 00:03:40,658
Well, looks like Shota's
job is officially done.

31
00:03:40,741 --> 00:03:42,618
See even after that she won't smile.

32
00:03:42,701 --> 00:03:43,577
Right?!

33
00:03:47,915 --> 00:03:53,087
As for Kazehaya... I thought that
I had become much closer to him...

34
00:04:03,389 --> 00:04:09,478
But ever since our seats became farther
apart, I feel like we've also grown apart.

35
00:04:12,523 --> 00:04:14,358
Then, it was February.

36
00:04:16,360 --> 00:04:17,861
Oh, that's right.

37
00:04:17,945 --> 00:04:21,657
I don't really eat sweets a whole lot,
but I'll still take whatever ya give me.

38
00:04:21,740 --> 00:04:25,703
And tomorrow is Valentine's Day.

39
00:04:26,036 --> 00:04:28,747
So, are you gonna make some? Or buy?

40
00:04:29,873 --> 00:04:30,457
Chocolates.

41
00:04:32,334 --> 00:04:35,671
What are you so surprised about? I
figured you make some for your dad every

42
00:04:35,754 --> 00:04:39,008
- year, knowing you.
- My... dad...

43
00:04:40,175 --> 00:04:43,304
- And you?
- I'm planning to give some to

44
00:04:43,387 --> 00:04:44,972
Ryu. What about you Yano-chin?

45
00:04:45,055 --> 00:04:46,640
Let's see... I was thinking a
bribe doesn't sound too bad.

46
00:04:46,724 --> 00:04:49,810
What do you mean "a bribe"?

47
00:04:49,893 --> 00:04:54,732
Truth is... I'd already prepared
all the ingredients in advance.

48
00:05:03,365 --> 00:05:06,327
This one here will be for Ayane.

49
00:05:06,410 --> 00:05:11,749
There's one for Chizu and Sanada to
share. And one for Tomo and for Ekko too.

50
00:05:12,541 --> 00:05:15,753
This one's for my dad and...

51
00:05:20,299 --> 00:05:21,925
This one's for...

52
00:05:26,638 --> 00:05:29,016
A- Actually, forget about the card.

53
00:05:37,566 --> 00:05:41,320
Huh? When I look closely, the ones for
Kazehaya have more nuts than any of the

54
00:05:41,403 --> 00:05:45,199
others. Huh? It's the same with the
heart-shaped decorations. I sprinkled way

55
00:05:45,282 --> 00:05:47,743
more of them on his!

56
00:05:49,078 --> 00:05:52,247
I- I've been subconsciously favoring him!

57
00:05:52,915 --> 00:05:55,584
On top of that, they're homemade.

58
00:05:56,210 --> 00:05:58,796
I want to give him homemade ones...

59
00:06:00,130 --> 00:06:06,011
If I gave them as a thank-you gift for
all he's done... would that be too much?

60
00:06:06,887 --> 00:06:07,721
But...

61
00:06:15,145 --> 00:06:17,022
Either way, I want to.

62
00:06:19,983 --> 00:06:21,652
For sure this time.

63
00:06:40,295 --> 00:06:43,382
- Uh, morning.
- Good morning.

64
00:06:47,553 --> 00:06:50,639
Th-Those were chocolates, weren't they?

65
00:06:51,432 --> 00:06:53,392
Well, yeah, of course.

66
00:07:03,193 --> 00:07:03,986
Uhh, see ya!

67
00:07:04,695 --> 00:07:05,487
B- Bye!

68
00:07:17,207 --> 00:07:19,501
I couldn't give them to him.

69
00:07:20,294 --> 00:07:23,630
- D-D-Delicious! Okay!
- Please eat them with

70
00:07:23,714 --> 00:07:27,634
- together with Sanada.
- Thanks so much!

71
00:07:27,718 --> 00:07:29,887
- Yeah, thank you, Sadako!
- Yeah, thank you, Sadako!

72
00:07:29,970 --> 00:07:32,181
I think you've got great potential.

73
00:07:32,264 --> 00:07:34,141
Well, I'm glad everyone's happy with them.

74
00:07:35,726 --> 00:07:37,561
- The last one's for...
- Kazehaya! I've got some chocolates.

75
00:07:37,644 --> 00:07:39,480
Too good. Way too good.

76
00:07:39,563 --> 00:07:41,315
Oh! Thank you.

77
00:07:42,191 --> 00:07:44,902
- Friendship chocolates!
- That's for sure.

78
00:07:45,194 --> 00:07:48,113
Look at them, enjoying it so innocently.

79
00:07:51,992 --> 00:07:54,661
I-I'm going to the restroom!

80
00:07:56,330 --> 00:07:57,206
Sawako?

81
00:08:02,920 --> 00:08:06,215
I'm so nervous. I just don't know anymore.

82
00:08:06,798 --> 00:08:11,428
I mean, since this morning, I've already
seen him receive two chocolates. If I gave

83
00:08:11,512 --> 00:08:15,891
him some too, wouldn't
it spike his blood sugar?

84
00:08:15,974 --> 00:08:20,062
It's not like he has to eat them all in
one day. He could leave some in the

85
00:08:20,145 --> 00:08:24,566
fridge. Then it wouldn't be a problem.

86
00:08:24,650 --> 00:08:29,279
If I could just give it to him as
naturally and friendly as she did, maybe

87
00:08:29,363 --> 00:08:31,949
he'd happily accept them the same
way. I got some chocolates here for you!

88
00:08:32,032 --> 00:08:33,784
Oh, thank you!

89
00:08:35,744 --> 00:08:38,914
Th- That might be even more unnatural...

90
00:08:41,583 --> 00:08:47,548
That's right, just give them to him like
you did with Chizu and Ayane. Normally.

91
00:08:48,674 --> 00:08:49,675
Normally?

92
00:08:50,717 --> 00:08:52,803
- What's that?!
- What's that?!

93
00:08:52,886 --> 00:08:56,598
It's no use. Every time I think about
giving Kazehaya chocolates, I become so

94
00:08:56,682 --> 00:08:59,893
incredibly self-conscious.

95
00:09:03,647 --> 00:09:06,733
- Oh. You got some too, Ryu?
- Here.

96
00:09:07,985 --> 00:09:14,908
Oh, hey, thanks. Woah, there's
something kinda different about this one.

97
00:09:14,992 --> 00:09:18,453
Are you sure it was okay for me to eat
that? Were these supposed to be for you?

98
00:09:18,537 --> 00:09:21,707
Nah, don't worry. Chizuru just gave--

99
00:09:21,790 --> 00:09:26,795
- Yoshida made these?
- No way. They're Kuronuma's homemade ones.

100
00:09:28,755 --> 00:09:33,260
So, yeah, they're friendship
chocolates passed down to me. You okay?

101
00:09:39,057 --> 00:09:40,809
She has them too!

102
00:09:40,892 --> 00:09:46,148
What's up? You want some? I
suppose I can share then.

103
00:09:46,231 --> 00:09:47,357
- I'm good!
- Shota.

104
00:09:49,192 --> 00:09:50,110
Company.

105
00:09:56,658 --> 00:09:59,620
Am I just overthinking all of this?

106
00:10:00,495 --> 00:10:04,625
If we still had our old seats, would I
have been able to naturally give them to

107
00:10:04,708 --> 00:10:08,837
him like I did with everyone else?

108
00:10:25,729 --> 00:10:28,315
- I saw it! The whole thing!
- It looked like he rejected her.

109
00:10:28,398 --> 00:10:29,232
Whaaat?!

110
00:10:29,316 --> 00:10:31,485
That's a waste if you ask me.

111
00:10:31,568 --> 00:10:35,364
Rejected... I see. That's
a possible outcome too.

112
00:10:46,166 --> 00:10:49,711
But that was different.
Hers meant more, right?

113
00:10:50,962 --> 00:10:53,674
"It began with calculation and
misunderstanding." -"Now that I've snapped

114
00:10:53,757 --> 00:10:56,468
out of my daydreams... I can see everything
so much more clearly than before." -Was he

115
00:10:56,551 --> 00:10:59,262
happily accepting those chocolates
earlier... Only because they were the

116
00:10:59,346 --> 00:11:01,348
friendship kind?

117
00:11:02,057 --> 00:11:04,601
Mine are a token of gratitude...

118
00:11:05,310 --> 00:11:10,065
But do thank- you gifts...
count as friendship? Sympathy?

119
00:11:10,148 --> 00:11:14,861
Huh? I wasn't intending to
confess my feelings or anything.

120
00:11:14,945 --> 00:11:19,616
But I do feel that way about
him... there's no question there.

121
00:11:21,159 --> 00:11:23,829
In this case, what do these mean?

122
00:11:24,746 --> 00:11:26,164
He rejected her...

123
00:11:34,131 --> 00:11:36,091
Reality... just hit me.

124
00:11:40,929 --> 00:11:43,515
I want to give these to him...

125
00:11:43,598 --> 00:11:47,227
And if I'm going to do
it, it needs to be soon.

126
00:11:48,019 --> 00:11:51,022
Wait, H- how is school over already?!

127
00:11:53,859 --> 00:11:55,610
- Well, I'm glad you got to give it to him.
- I'm totally hooked on

128
00:11:55,694 --> 00:11:57,446
- this tv drama's re-run!!
- It looked like he was

129
00:11:57,529 --> 00:11:59,030
- happy with it as well.
- Really? One of those foreign dramas?

130
00:11:59,114 --> 00:12:00,657
Uh-uh, a "trendy drama."

131
00:12:02,826 --> 00:12:08,665
Hold on, has this girl even given them
to him? It sure doesn't seem like it.

132
00:12:08,749 --> 00:12:10,959
Now, let's go. I am
ready to get outta here.

133
00:12:11,042 --> 00:12:11,877
Uhh...

134
00:12:14,004 --> 00:12:17,299
- You guys wanna go hang out somewhere?
- Uhh, can't. Got plans with my girlfriend.

135
00:12:17,382 --> 00:12:20,677
I'm gonna stay after a little
longer. I'll head home by myself later.

136
00:12:20,761 --> 00:12:22,763
H- He's leaving.

137
00:12:23,722 --> 00:12:25,223
Hiya, Shota!

138
00:12:27,058 --> 00:12:29,853
I got a nice little job for ya! Come here!

139
00:12:30,395 --> 00:12:32,230
- Kazehaya!
- Kazehaya!

140
00:12:32,314 --> 00:12:34,566
You guys head home without him!

141
00:12:34,649 --> 00:12:35,776
Kazehaya...

142
00:12:36,067 --> 00:12:38,612
- Why's it hafta be me?
- Because it does.

143
00:12:38,695 --> 00:12:40,572
That's all you need to know.

144
00:12:40,655 --> 00:12:42,574
He'll still be at school.

145
00:12:48,121 --> 00:12:50,499
This could be my last chance.

146
00:12:53,835 --> 00:12:55,420
Sorry. Actually...

147
00:12:57,005 --> 00:12:59,674
Do you two mind going home without me?

148
00:13:00,509 --> 00:13:03,220
I think... I'm gonna stay a bit longer.

149
00:13:05,013 --> 00:13:09,100
- Huh? Then we can stay after to--
- Nah, it's fine. C'mon, let her do

150
00:13:09,184 --> 00:13:11,603
her thing. We'll see you tomorrow then!

151
00:13:11,686 --> 00:13:13,688
Huh? Well, okay.

152
00:13:14,147 --> 00:13:16,733
Oh, so check it out, Joe's
been eyeing you for a while now.

153
00:13:16,817 --> 00:13:19,820
Shh! Don't make eye contact!

154
00:13:19,903 --> 00:13:20,737
H-Hey...

155
00:13:30,580 --> 00:13:32,415
I ended up staying...

156
00:13:32,958 --> 00:13:35,627
But what should I do? I'm scared.

157
00:13:38,088 --> 00:13:41,299
Well, you see, lately, my shoulders have
been getting kinda stiff. So I could use a

158
00:13:41,383 --> 00:13:43,260
strong massage.

159
00:13:45,053 --> 00:13:48,056
No way. You dragged me here for that?

160
00:13:48,139 --> 00:13:52,227
You should feel honored that I asked you.
You don't have to if you don't want to.

161
00:13:52,310 --> 00:13:56,398
But remember a long time ago, when you
showed up to my house crying during a rain

162
00:13:56,481 --> 00:13:57,315
storm?

163
00:13:59,234 --> 00:14:02,195
Dad told me I had to... bring this to you.

164
00:14:02,279 --> 00:14:05,365
Are you scared of the storm or something?

165
00:14:05,448 --> 00:14:08,326
Remember how you whined and cried,
insisting that you wanted to spend the

166
00:14:08,410 --> 00:14:10,078
night at my house? Then you
ended up wetting the futon.

167
00:14:10,161 --> 00:14:11,955
This juice is yummy.

168
00:14:12,038 --> 00:14:17,085
You're such a little gremlin! I'll take
a picture. -So, you don't have to, but I

169
00:14:17,168 --> 00:14:22,132
don't have to not share that for
announcements- -Okay, I get it!

170
00:14:22,924 --> 00:14:25,552
Ah, nice. Especially the back
of my neck and my left shoulder...

171
00:14:25,635 --> 00:14:26,761
You suck.

172
00:14:31,308 --> 00:14:36,062
- What's that?
- Ah, you mean those chocolates?

173
00:14:36,146 --> 00:14:38,857
When you're this popular, the
fangirls never leave ya alone.

174
00:14:38,940 --> 00:14:41,693
Ah, he just wanted to brag
about this. He's a total jerk.

175
00:14:41,776 --> 00:14:44,487
It can be a real pain.

176
00:14:47,157 --> 00:14:49,618
Wait, that bag of
chocolates! Is that from Kuronuma?!

177
00:14:49,701 --> 00:14:50,952
You idiot.

178
00:14:52,370 --> 00:14:56,124
Why would I tell you? You'd never catch
me sayin' somethin' that might end up

179
00:14:56,541 --> 00:15:00,670
breaking a girl's heart! I bet you feel
like total crap, but don't be too jealous!

180
00:15:00,754 --> 00:15:05,300
- Ouch! That's my bone right there!
- The back of your neck and your left

181
00:15:05,383 --> 00:15:09,930
shoulder? Maybe it's a curse or something.

182
00:15:10,013 --> 00:15:13,391
There was a manga I read that said any
pain or illness above the neck is related

183
00:15:13,475 --> 00:15:16,895
- to the gods.
- Uh... the gods?

184
00:15:18,313 --> 00:15:20,190
I took my anger out on the shrine's
divine tree... Damn it all! This! Sucks!

185
00:15:20,273 --> 00:15:21,149
Stupid!

186
00:15:22,192 --> 00:15:26,696
I cheaped out with my offering too. I
don't got any change on me, but oh well.

187
00:15:30,200 --> 00:15:35,956
I gotta hurry and cleanse myself with
Kuronuma's chocolates! Sh-Shota! Water!

188
00:15:36,039 --> 00:15:41,544
- Water!
- With the wrappers?! Oh, he's choking.

189
00:16:23,712 --> 00:16:26,381
If I'm going to give him these...

190
00:16:27,549 --> 00:16:29,217
Now's my only chance.

191
00:16:31,011 --> 00:16:33,179
- Kaze--
- Kazehaya.

192
00:16:35,432 --> 00:16:36,391
Kurumi?!

193
00:16:38,476 --> 00:16:39,602
Kurumizawa. Hey.

194
00:16:42,105 --> 00:16:47,402
I was hoping you'd accept this for
Valentine's day, just so I could have the

195
00:16:47,485 --> 00:16:52,824
memory. That much should be okay, right?
Since this'll be the first and last time.

196
00:17:01,750 --> 00:17:02,667
Thank you.

197
00:17:30,570 --> 00:17:32,614
Spying? That's not very nice!

198
00:17:33,198 --> 00:17:38,119
I-I-I-I-I'm sorry! I got kinda,
really, very, extremely curious.

199
00:17:38,203 --> 00:17:39,829
She admitted it!

200
00:17:48,004 --> 00:17:52,759
He won't... accept chocolate
from someone who likes him.

201
00:17:55,011 --> 00:17:56,971
Then what about yours?

202
00:17:57,514 --> 00:18:00,058
Mine are kind of a special case.

203
00:18:01,226 --> 00:18:03,895
I was already flat out rejected, so...

204
00:18:06,272 --> 00:18:08,358
You see? Special.

205
00:18:13,822 --> 00:18:15,490
So... are those for him?

206
00:18:16,241 --> 00:18:18,743
Uhh, th-these are my
way of saying thank you!

207
00:18:18,827 --> 00:18:21,621
I can't help but wonder...

208
00:18:21,704 --> 00:18:24,624
You once said something like you'd never
think of going out with him, but are you

209
00:18:24,707 --> 00:18:27,752
positive? Just a thank-you?

210
00:18:29,754 --> 00:18:34,300
Are you sure there's not a
deeper meaning... if there's a chance?

211
00:18:37,929 --> 00:18:41,558
Think about those chocolates... If
they're friendship ones, then I'm sure

212
00:18:41,641 --> 00:18:45,270
that Kazehaya will accept them.

213
00:18:48,606 --> 00:18:51,860
But I just hope that you
don't regret it. See ya.

214
00:18:54,612 --> 00:18:57,240
If you can't get over me teasing you a
little, then it'll never work out anyway.

215
00:18:57,323 --> 00:18:59,659
If it isn't Kurumi!

216
00:19:01,035 --> 00:19:02,829
Y'know... I didn't get any
chocolates from you yet.

217
00:19:02,912 --> 00:19:04,038
Oh. Yeah.

218
00:19:07,250 --> 00:19:11,171
- And we're classmates! How cold!
- But seriously, she's changed a lot

219
00:19:11,254 --> 00:19:14,424
lately. She used to be so nice and cute.

220
00:19:14,507 --> 00:19:17,677
- Don'tcha think she's better like this?
- Nope. I liked her better before.

221
00:19:17,760 --> 00:19:21,306
- You're so close- minded.
- What, you're fine with any

222
00:19:21,389 --> 00:19:22,849
girl as long as they're cute?

223
00:19:22,932 --> 00:19:24,726
I mean, girls are just
cute in general, ya know?

224
00:19:24,809 --> 00:19:26,519
Nah, not all of them.

225
00:19:36,946 --> 00:19:40,325
- Just now, wasn't that Class D's...
- Ah, Sadako?

226
00:19:40,408 --> 00:19:44,454
Yeah, her! The girl everyone talks about...
So even girls like her think about giving

227
00:19:44,537 --> 00:19:46,414
out chocolates.

228
00:19:54,339 --> 00:19:57,342
A thank-you gift... Is just an excuse.

229
00:20:02,180 --> 00:20:04,474
I didn't mean to, but man...

230
00:20:06,226 --> 00:20:10,897
Seems like I was expecting
something. Way more than I thought.

231
00:20:11,814 --> 00:20:16,027
All that anxiety... came from
secretly hoping for more.

232
00:20:17,195 --> 00:20:21,115
If they're friendship ones,
I'm sure he'll accept them.

